    {
      "id": "f48f0b13132dca393be64651aec8321081027c45",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 464534629,
          "type": null,
          "body": "My general solution to all situations where there isn't a simple way to fix up a Git problem is [\"nuke it from orbit, it's the only way to be sure\"](https://xkcd.com/1597/).\n\nIf GitLab and my repository were that much out of phase, I'd probably close the old merge request with a \"DO NOT EVER REVIVE THIS\" note, check out a fresh local repository, create a branch (I have a git-reviewbranch script to make this less painful), commit the updated change, push it to my GitLab holding area repository (I have a git-doreview script to make this less painful), and then create a brand new merge request.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
